<document lang="en" type="presentation" theme-accent="purple">
  <title>Delta decks</title>

  <progress/>

  <slide>
    <toc label="Plan">
      <title>Plan</title>
    </toc>
  </slide>
  <section>
    <title>Part One — The Basics</title>
    <slide>
      <title>Presentations in Delta</title>
      The same strict-XML source, compiled to a single offline HTML file — now paged
      at projector scale. Use the arrow keys to move between slides.
    </slide>

    <slide>
      <title>Math still works</title>
      Inline math like $e^{i\pi} + 1 = 0$ renders as usual, and display math is
      centered and large — press → to reveal it:
      <equation id="eq:gauss" reveal="true">\int_{-\infty}^{\infty} e^{-x^2}\,dx = \sqrt{\pi}</equation>
    </slide>

  </section>
  
  <section>
    <title>Part Two — Going Deeper</title>

    <slide>
      <title>Theorems on a slide</title>
      <theorem id="thm:pyth">
        <title>Pythagoras</title>
        For a right triangle with legs $a$, $b$ and hypotenuse $c$,
        <equation id="eq:pyth">a^2 + b^2 = c^2</equation>
      </theorem>
    </slide>

    <slide>
      <title>Ordinary chrome, deck scale</title>
      Lists and emphasis all carry over — revealed one point at a time with a single
      <c>animated="true"</c> on the list:
      <list marker="number" animated="true">
        <item>Built from the same tags you already know.</item>
        <item>Each &lt;slide&gt; fills the screen, its title at the top.</item>
        <item>Still a single, fully offline file.</item>
      </list>
    </slide>
  </section>
</document>
